# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Aphrodite .gitignore
# Organized by category. Patterns are ordered so re-includes come AFTER the
# exclusion they override (gitignore semantics: a negation inside an excluded
# directory is a no-op unless the directory itself is re-included first).
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Rust / Cargo ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bare `target/` (no leading slash) matches build dirs at ANY depth - root,
# bench/compression, Maintain/dynamic_hooks/rust, etc.
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.eggs/
*.egg
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Python tool caches
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ── Hermes / dev artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Re-include against a machine-global excludesFile that ignores `.hermes`
# (verified via `git check-ignore -v`: the repo's .gitignore is checked AFTER
# core.excludesFile, so a repo-level negation can override it - but a leading
# `./` is not valid gitignore syntax and never matched anything; a prior
# "restore" of this line kept the same dead pattern under a mistaken
# diagnosis). `.hermes` is the tracked dev archive - never ignore it.
!.hermes/
!.hermes/**

.headroom/
*.log
*.lock
*.tar.gz

# ── Profiles - keep local, ship only examples ───────────────────────────────
# `dir/` + `!dir/sub/` never re-includes anything below an excluded directory
# (report 12 F7) - the correct shape is `dir/*` plus explicit re-includes for
# both the subdirectory entry and its contents.
profiles/*
!profiles/example/
!profiles/example/**

# ── Test artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
plugins/aphrodite/.test-results.json

# ── Aphrodite proxy binary (copied to profile/plugin dirs at build) ────────
plugins/aphrodite/aphrodite

# ── Local config (not committed) ────────────────────────────────────────────
aphrodite.toml
aphrodite.local.toml

# ── IDE / editors ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
# .vscode is excluded EXCEPT settings.json, which is shared. The bare
# `!.vscode/settings.json` under an excluded dir is a no-op; re-include the
# dir first, re-exclude its contents, then re-include the file.
!.vscode/
.vscode/**
!.vscode/settings.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── JS / pnpm ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
pnpm-lock.yaml

# ── Secrets (never commit) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.sh
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# ── Catch-all leaks / runtime state ──────────────────────────────────────────
**/state.db*
**/auth.json
**/auth.lock
**/.hermes_*
**/.skills_*
**/.update_check
**/.DS_Sccp_*.txt
.cargo_check_output.txt

# ── Benchmark outputs (machine-generated; never tracked) ────────────────────
bench/conversational/results/
bench/conversational/__pycache__/
bench/results/proxy-bench-*-*.json
bench/results/tmp/bench-rendered.toml
bench/results/tmp/ccr-bench.db
bench/results/tmp/ccr-bench.db-shm
bench/results/tmp/ccr-bench.db-wal
bench/results/wire-compat-*-*.json

# ── Misc ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
placeholder/
.bench